\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Overall functional system architecture, illustrating data ingestion across three corpora, shared utterance encoding, the dual-stream Antiphony intention network, and the 19-member multi-task strategy classification framework with calibrated decision blending.}}{18}{figure.caption.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Persuasion strategy annotation pipeline, depicting contextual batching (200 turns per batch, 5-turn history), the 4-tier decision protocol, LLM agent annotation under human checkpoints, automated schema validation, and multi-label compilation into \texttt {multilabel\textunderscore \penalty 0\relax merged.jsonl}.}}{19}{figure.caption.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Three-pass intention annotation lineage, showing the initial 738/279 binary split with modifier, the second pass deprecating the modifier, and the third pass enforcing strict unconditional commitment (694 yes / 323 no via two-step re-checking).}}{22}{figure.caption.14}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces Three-phase synthetic negotiation benchmark generation pipeline, comprising persona-conditioned LLM drafting ($N=500$ canonical, $N=200$ adversarial reversals), organic paraphrasing with linguistic jitter, and multi-tier semantic audit.}}{23}{figure.caption.15}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.5}{\ignorespaces Strategy and category classification framework, illustrating the 19-member model pool, multi-task representation heads, and decision layer search comparing calibrated power-mean blending (selected, val macro-F1 0.5716) against XGBoost stacking (tested, val macro-F1 0.5508).}}{25}{figure.caption.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.6}{\ignorespaces The AntiphonyClassifier (v14) neural architecture: raw turns undergo batched utterance encoding, masked mean-pooling, and role-pure splitting ($R=20$). Persuader and Decider streams pass through independent 2-layer Transformers. The Decider stream queries the Persuader stream via directional cross-attention. Contextualized Decider states are aggregated in parallel by a commitment-trajectory GRU (read at the true final Decider turn) and attention pooling, followed by latent concatenation and Class-Balanced Focal classification.}}{28}{figure.caption.17}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.7}{\ignorespaces Four-stage architectural evolution of intention classification models (v1 through v14), depicting key innovations, critical bug diagnoses, and peak test Macro-F1 across stages.}}{30}{figure.caption.18}%
